<services>
  <!-- OBS pulls EVERYTHING itself; `_service` is the only file committed to OBS.
       Same shape as every other tool in this lane — see opensuse/README.md.

       1. download_url fetches the SPEC straight from `main` of the packaging
          repo, so git stays the single source of truth. Only the spec: it is the
          one file that cannot fetch itself. Every other recipe file carries a
          URL in its own Source: line and is pulled by download_files in step 2.

          That split is deliberate. This file lives in OBS and only an
          `osc commit` can change it. No token can, and nothing automates it.
          Listing recipe files here would make _service a function of our file
          list, so adding one would need a hand in OBS; forgetting that hand
          surfaces as `broken: service error: ERROR 404`, which reads like an OBS
          outage and is really our own dangling reference. As it stands now,
          _service depends on the PACKAGE NAME only and never has to change again.

          (No double hyphens anywhere above: XML forbids them inside a comment
          and OBS rejects the whole file for it. Warned about below, and writing
          this very paragraph still tripped over it once.)
       2. download_files then reads the *generated* spec and downloads the upstream
          assets named in its Source: URLs (the pinned b729 release zip, LICENSE,
          README). OBS build roots have no network, so they must exist as package
          sources before the build starts.

       The services run SERVER-SIDE (no mode= attribute), so a scoped `runservice`
       token can refresh the package (.github/workflows/obs-trigger.yml). An OBS
       token can never commit — which is precisely why the recipe has to be fetched
       by OBS rather than pushed to it.

       Unlike the rolling `redumper`, nothing here ever moves: the build number is
       pinned in the name. The service exists so the RECIPE can be corrected from
       git, not so the binary can advance. -->
  <service name="download_url">
    <param name="url">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gmipf/packaging-media-preservation/main/opensuse/redumper-mpf/redumper-mpf.spec</param>
    <param name="filename">redumper-mpf.spec</param>
  </service>
  <!-- upstream assets, taken from the Source: URLs of the spec above -->
  <service name="download_files"/>
  <!-- BEGIN deb · generated by scripts/obs/gen-deb.sh · do not edit by hand.
       Keep double hyphens out of this comment: XML forbids them inside a
       comment, and OBS then rejects the whole _service file, not just it.

       No upstream archive is fetched here. download_files above already pulled
       the spec's Source: URLs, and the .dsc names those very files: the RPM and
       the .deb are built from the same upstream bytes, downloaded once. -->
  <service name="download_url">
    <param name="url">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gmipf/packaging-media-preservation/main/opensuse/redumper-mpf/redumper-mpf.dsc</param>
    <param name="filename">redumper-mpf.dsc</param>
  </service>
  <service name="download_url">
    <param name="url">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gmipf/packaging-media-preservation/main/opensuse/redumper-mpf/debian.tar.gz</param>
    <param name="filename">debian.tar.gz</param>
  </service>
  <service name="download_url">
    <param name="url">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gmipf/packaging-media-preservation/main/ubuntu/redumper-mpf/debian/changelog</param>
    <param name="filename">debian.changelog</param>
  </service>
  <!-- END deb -->
</services>
